SwiftPutty local patch 0008
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   reported upstream (2026-10-19); should be (memory safety)

Fix a use after free when two configured remote port forwardings map to
the same server listening address (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md section 5.6,
hazard H-2).

In portfwdmgr_config()'s create pass, when ssh_rportfwd_alloc() returns
NULL because another remote forwarding already uses the same server
address and port (for example "R8080" alongside "4R8080", which differ
only in address family), the new PortFwdRecord was freed but left in
mgr->forwardings. The next portfwdmgr_config() (any reconfiguration) or
portfwdmgr_free() then walked the freed record. Reproduced under
AddressSanitizer (Core/tests/spb_ssh_test.c).

Remove it from the tree before freeing it, as the destroy pass does,
stepping the loop index back so no record is skipped.

--- a/ssh/portfwd.c
+++ b/ssh/portfwd.c
@@ -1054,6 +1054,11 @@
                               "Duplicate remote port forwarding to %s:%d",
                               pfr->daddr, pfr->dport);
                     portfwdmgr_report_status(mgr, pfr, PFS_DUPLICATE, NULL);
+                    /* Out of the tree first, or the next
+                     * portfwdmgr_config() or portfwdmgr_free() would
+                     * find the freed record there. */
+                    delpos234(mgr->forwardings, i);
+                    i--;           /* so we don't skip one in the list */
                     pfr_free(pfr);
                 } else {
                     logeventf(mgr->cl->logctx, "Requesting remote port %s"
